\" Generated by script2man from auto-service-enabled
.TH auto-service-enabled 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-service-enabled - Exit 0 if the indicated service is enables

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-service-enabled service-name
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
service-name    Name of the service (as spelled in rc.conf, etc.)
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-service-enabled
command exits with 0 (success) status if "service-name" is
currently enabled.  This is meant to be run in conditionals
in scripts.

Note: The service name used here is the name of the service
indicated in /etc/rc.conf, which may differ from the filename
of the service script in /etc/rc.conf.
For example, on FreeBSD, the service name for /etc/rc.d/lockd
is "rpc_lockd".

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 if the service is enabled, non-zero otherwise

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
if auto-service-enabled sshd; then
    ...
fi
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8)

